CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --enforce-contract sum
^\[count_pos\.assigns\.\d+\] line 5 Check that \*count is assignable: SUCCESS$
^\[count_pos\.assigns\.\d+\] line 9 Check that \*count is assignable: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^\[.*\] .*: FAILURE$
--
Functions called in contract clauses are instrumented, and assignments to their
own local variables, also via pointers in functions that they call, must not be
reported as side effects of the requires clause.
